comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-08T09:58:16.116Z","harness:codex","Duplicate-check evidence: all-status exact-title search returned zero items; broader @types/node and ESLint searches found closed historical refreshes and canonical npm-package-arg 14 deferment pm-ksr40d, but no item owns the 2026-08-08 compatible patch pair. Live outdated: @types/node 26.1.2 -> 26.2.0, eslint 10.8.0 -> 10.8.1; TypeScript 7 remains a separate major."
  "2026-08-08T10:00:11.492Z","harness:codex","Dependency disposition: @types/node 26.2.0 and ESLint 10.8.1 were published only about 19 hours ago. pnpm correctly required new minimumReleaseAgeExclude bypasses to install them; those generated exceptions and the dependency changes were removed rather than weakening the supply-chain gate. npm-package-arg 14 remains owned by pm-ksr40d and incompatible with the published Node 22 floor. pnpm audit is zero. Resume this item after the three-day cooldown."
  "2026-08-08T15:40:17.587Z","harness:codex","2026-08-08 refresh evidence: pnpm outdated has no compatible wanted-version updates; only the separately tracked npm-package-arg 14 and TypeScript 7 majors remain. GitHub Dependabot, code-scanning, and secret-scanning open-alert APIs all returned empty arrays; pnpm audit is 0/0/0/0/0."
  "2026-08-09T00:17:44.465Z","harness:codex","Dependency sweep evidence (2026-08-09): npm outdated now reports compatible wanted updates @types/node 26.1.2 -> 26.2.0 and eslint 10.8.0 -> 10.8.1, published 2026-08-07T17:52:07Z and 2026-08-07T20:21:24Z respectively. Both remain inside this repository's 3-day minimumReleaseAge supply-chain window, so no bypass or temporary exclusion was added. esbuild 0.28.2 was published 2026-08-08T20:00:55Z and is outside the current exact wanted constraint; npm-package-arg 14 and TypeScript 7 remain separately tracked major migrations. pnpm audit reports zero info/low/moderate/high/critical vulnerabilities across 357 dependencies; GitHub Dependabot, code-scanning, and secret-scanning alert APIs were also empty. Leave this canonical item open and unclaimed until the compatible versions age through policy."
